# Example crontab for the server-side (ws7) deployment.
# Install with:  crontab crontab.example
# Inspect with:  crontab -l
# Edit with:     crontab -e
#
# Paths assume the repo is at /tmp2/b12902066/Gym_Fetch. If your CSIE
# account differs, adjust the ID in PATH and in the paths below.

SHELL=/bin/bash
# Rootless docker lives under /tmp2/<id>/docker/bin and is NOT on the default
# cron PATH — prepend it so tools/sync_local.sh and the render job can find
# the `docker` binary. (DOCKER_HOST is derived automatically by
# tools/psql_gym_postgres.sh, so it does not need to be set here.)
PATH=/tmp2/b12902066/docker/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
MAILTO=

# The pipeline is staggered so each stage runs after the previous one:
#   :00 fetch  ->  :02 sync sqlite->postgres  ->  :04 render public page
# New occupancy readings reach the public page within ~4-5 minutes.
#
# Every job runs through tools/cronlog.sh, which appends combined stdout +
# stderr to a per-day file:  logs/<YYYY-MM>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<name>.log
# (<name> = cron / sync / render) — split by date, grouped by month.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Collector: fetch_counts.py every 5 minutes during sports-center open
#    hours. The script's own --open-hours-only flag double-checks, so the
#    cron windows can be slightly conservative. --no-log-file disables its
#    built-in daily log — cronlog.sh already writes the dated file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/5 6-21 * * 1-5 cd /tmp2/b12902066/Gym_Fetch && tools/cronlog.sh cron /usr/bin/python3 fetch_counts.py --open-hours-only --no-log-file
*/5 9-21 * * 6   cd /tmp2/b12902066/Gym_Fetch && tools/cronlog.sh cron /usr/bin/python3 fetch_counts.py --open-hours-only --no-log-file
*/5 9-17 * * 0   cd /tmp2/b12902066/Gym_Fetch && tools/cronlog.sh cron /usr/bin/python3 fetch_counts.py --open-hours-only --no-log-file

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Sync sqlite -> postgres every 5 minutes, 2 min after each fetch.
#    tools/sync_local.sh sources .env, so the postgres URL is not hard-coded
#    here. Idempotent upsert — harmless when there is nothing new.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
2-59/5 * * * * cd /tmp2/b12902066/Gym_Fetch && tools/cronlog.sh sync tools/sync_local.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Public page: regenerate the interactive static dashboard every 5 minutes,
#    4 min after each fetch (2 min after the sync), into ~/htdocs/gym/ so
#    nginx UserDir serves it as https://www.csie.ntu.edu.tw/~b12902066/gym/
#    Pure stdlib + psql — no headless browser needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
4-59/5 * * * * cd /tmp2/b12902066/Gym_Fetch && tools/cronlog.sh render /usr/bin/python3 tools/render_public_html.py --output-dir ~/htdocs/gym --psql tools/psql_gym_postgres.sh
